From 064a018fe9ddf29414e3b2a5930468c40a1f56c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Richardson <Alexander.Richardson@cl.cam.ac.uk>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 17:03:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] compiler-rt: Backport the ARM inexact status-bit correction

Adapt upstream LLVM e2cd2f7d08ce4391f19c0ce5c4ea63bb9a985fcf to
Android 12 clang-r416183b1 (12.0.7) ARM builtins archives.

__fe_raise_inexact currently sets FPSCR IXE (0x1000), enabling a trap,
instead of the cumulative inexact status IXC (0x10). Preserve the
Android 11 migration fix when replacing the compiler prebuilt.

Replace only ORR r0,r0,#4096 with ORR r0,r0,#16 in fp_mode.c.o.
Two bytes per archive change; archive lengths, indices and all other
members remain unchanged. Correct both exported/regular builtins and
the NDK runtime copy; no floating-point exception masking is added.

Upstream: https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/commit/e2cd2f7d08ce4391f19c0ce5c4ea63bb9a985fcf
Test: disassemble all three archives; verify exactly two changed bytes
per archive. Build and phone validation are recorded separately.

Change-Id: I7563e776c38436b4c7d9395682e1ebe5e4ac660d
